  "number": 6047,
  "title": "Keep Web Chat's styles when a React 19.2 Activity hides and shows it",
  "body": "> Web Chat loses its styles when a React 19.2 `<Activity>` hides and shows it.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed styles lost after a React 19.2 `<Activity>` hides and shows Web Chat, in PR [#6047](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6047), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nWhen a React 19.2 `<Activity>` hid Web Chat, the effect cleanup removed its emotion `<style>` elements; showing it did not add them back, as the reference count was taken in render. `useEmotion()` now counts in a layout effect and, after the last release, inserts the registered rules again.\n\n## Design\n\n- Rebuild from emotion's registered styles, not re-append the removed elements: production emotion uses `insertRule()`, whose rules are lost with the element, and classes created while hidden need rules too.\n- Effects cannot tell hiding from unmounting, so removal cannot wait for unmount. Not `@emotion/react` (never removes styles): CSS modules are replacing emotion.\n- Only mounted instances are shared: two Web Chats rendered in the same commit get two sheets.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `useEmotion.ts`: count in a layout effect, re-insert the registered rules after the last release\n- `react19/activity.hideShow{,.fluent,.styleOptions}.html`: same look after hide and show (default, Fluent), style options changed while hidden\n- `react19/strictMode.unmount.styles.html`, `strictMode/unmount.styles.html`: unmount removes the styles\n- `basic/twoWebChats.unmountOne.html`: the other Web Chat keeps the shared styles\n- `react19/activity.hideShow.sharedStyles.html`: shown again, then the other unmounts: styles kept\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
